      "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #61730: apply the missing decay step to incoming KV state during lightning-attention prefill, making long prompts and cached chunks consistent with the decode recurrence.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Correct output after the first 256-token block and from the first token when continuing from nonzero history.\n- Add 20 FP64-reference regression cases covering block boundaries, partial blocks, final KV state, and history preservation.\n\n## Validation\n\nTested on WSL with RTX 3050 OEM (8 GB), Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.14.0+cu132, and Triton 3.8.0, reusing existing compiled extensions.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| New regression cases before fix | 14 failed, 6 passed |\n| Complete attention test file after fix, default precision | 30 passed |\n| Complete attention test file with `TRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee` | 30 passed |\n| Real MiniMax prefill wrapper: 599 tokens, full prefill versus chunks 63/257/19/256 followed by four decode tokens; nonzero history, three seeds | Outputs and final states match FP64 recurrence; IEEE max absolute error / output RMS ≤ 4.8e-6 |\n| Repository pre-commit hooks, including mypy and test CI tethering | Passed |\n\nReproduce the committed regressions:\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_lightning_attn.py -q\nTRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee python -m pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_lightning_attn.py -q\npre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/layers/lightning_attn.py tests/kernels/attention/test_lightning_attn.py\n```\n\nRegression lengths: 1, 63, 64, 65, 255, 256, 257, 300, 512, and 769, with and without history; two batches, four slopes including zero. Comparisons use FP64 closed-form recurrence and per-head normalization with tolerance for default TF32 rounding.\n\nFull pretrained-model generation/quality evaluation was not run: the affected full models do not fit this 8 GB GPU. Validation covers the actual MiniMax prefill caller and decode transition, rather than a complete serving run. Head size 64 was tested; other head sizes and ROCm/XPU remain unvalidated.\n\n## Details\n\nThe incoming KV state represents the state immediately before the block. Its contribution to query position `c` therefore needs `exp(-s * (c + 1))`. The previous `exp(-s * c)` skipped one decay step, while diagonal attention and decode already followed the correct recurrence. The fix changes only this exponent; it adds no launch, allocation, synchronization, or interface changes.\n\nThe regression cases extend the existing attention suite. No performance improvement is claimed.\n\nDuplicate check: no open PR referencing #61730 or addressing this decay-index fix was found before submission. #41508 changes shared-memory sizing and addresses a different issue. The issue discussion includes another contributor expressing interest.\n\nAI assistance was used to implement and validate this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
